 "key_big": "a · b = |a||b| cos θ is a number; a × b is a vector.",
 "key_sub": "Area of a parallelogram = |a × b|; of a triangle = ½|a × b|.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><ul><li>For <b><i>a</i></b> = x î + y ĵ + z k̂: |<b><i>a</i></b>| = √(x² + y² + z²); unit vector â = <b><i>a</i></b> ÷ |<b><i>a</i></b>|; direction cosines x/|<b><i>a</i></b>|, y/|<b><i>a</i></b>|, z/|<b><i>a</i></b>|.</li><li>Vector AB = (position vector of B) − (position vector of A). The point dividing AB in the ratio m : n is (m<b>b</b> + n<b>a</b>) ÷ (m + n).</li><li><b><i>a</i></b> · <b><i>b</i></b> = a<sub>1</sub>b<sub>1</sub> + a<sub>2</sub>b<sub>2</sub> + a<sub>3</sub>b<sub>3</sub> = |<b><i>a</i></b>||<b><i>b</i></b>| cos θ; perpendicular vectors have <b><i>a</i></b> · <b><i>b</i></b> = 0. Projection of <b><i>a</i></b> on <b><i>b</i></b> = <b><i>a</i></b> · <b><i>b</i></b> ÷ |<b><i>b</i></b>|.</li><li><b><i>a</i></b> × <b><i>b</i></b> is found from a determinant; |<b><i>a</i></b> × <b><i>b</i></b>| is the area of the parallelogram on <b><i>a</i></b> and <b><i>b</i></b>.</li></ul><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Find the angle between î + ĵ and ĵ + k̂.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Dot product = 0 + 1 + 0 = 1</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>|a| = |b| = √2, so cos θ = 1/2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 60°</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Adding the components to get the magnitude.</li><li>Writing the vector AB as A − B.</li><li>Forgetting the ½ for the area of a triangle.</li></ul>",
